--- Surface ---
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ClimatePanel/ClimatePanel.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs (UI-free) +
ClimatePanel.cs (WinUI 3 ContentControl view). Parity port of
web/src/features/vehicles/components/telemetry-panels/ClimatePanel.tsx.

States reproduced (every web branch + the feature-view's own freshness chrome):
  loading (skeleton), loaded (temps + setpoints + HVAC + fan bars + system badges),
  empty ("No climate data available"), error (retry affordance), stale (chip + content), offline (chip + content).
  The web component is a pure child gated on truthy climateData; the native feature-view owns its
  cache-then-network /climate/latest read and therefore renders the full P2 state matrix.

Component mapping (web -> native): GlassPanel->TsGlassPanel, Thermometer icon->FontIcon (accent),
  MetricCard (Cabin/Outside)->TsMetricCard, setpoint/HVAC rows->Grid(label muted + mono value),
  six-bar fan indicator->graduated Borders (lit=accent / unlit=surface) + mono level, status chips->TsBadge(+FontIcon),
  FadeIn->TsFadeIn, skeleton/empty/error->TsSkeleton/TsEmptyState/TsQueryError, freshness->TsBadge+TsDataFreshness+TsButton.

Data sources (P1/S8): bound via the shared cache-then-network state-holder seam (IClimatePanelSource ->
  ClimatePanelSource -> CacheThenNetworkEngine over get_api_v1_climate_latest, scoped by vehicle_id;
  primary-vehicle resolution + disabled-when-no-vehicle short-circuit). The view performs no HTTP.
  Operation verified against the generated endpoint table (contract-drift guard test).

i18n (P1/S10): every string flows through the ILocalizer facade. All 13 source keys exist in
  apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json: common.climate, common.insideTemp, common.outsideTemp,
  telemetry.driverSetpoint, telemetry.passengerSetpoint, telemetry.hvacState, telemetry.fanSpeed,
  telemetry.defrost, common.off, common.on, telemetry.precondition, telemetry.climate, telemetry.noClimateData.
  English fallbacks asserted via PassthroughLocalizer (the repo's established fallback contract; resw is generated).

Units: SI degrees Celsius read straight from the API; converted to the user's preference only at the render
  boundary via UnitFormatters.FormatTemperature (web useUnits parity). Changing UnitPref re-projects the temps
  (asserted metric->imperial).

Accessibility: Narrator names on the panel, every metric/setpoint/HVAC row, the fan readout, each badge, and the
  refresh button; loading skeleton announced via LiveRegion; reduce-motion honoured on the skeleton; AutomationPeer
  reports a Group with the localized title.

